{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added an explicit `sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100)` prior for the already bounded parameter `sigma_a`. This is density-neutral for the original model because `sigma_a` was constrained to `[0, 100]` and otherwise had the corresponding implicit flat density. The prior is placed before `sigma_a` is used in the prior for `a`, satisfying SafeStan's parameter-use ordering rule. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> n_state;
  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[N] black;
  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[N] female;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=n_state> state;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> y;
}
parameters {
  vector[n_state] a;
  vector[2] b;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a;
  real mu_a;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[N] y_hat;

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = b[1] * black[i] + b[2] * female[i] + a[state[i]];
  }
}
model {
  mu_a ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100);
  a ~ normal(mu_a, sigma_a);
  b ~ normal(0, 100);
  y ~ bernoulli_logit(y_hat);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":3,"black":[0.9367015335034838,0.43505034952583455,0.8064622159990286],"female":[0.3889547507502962,0.30292686348057035,0.9402065557507667],"n_state":1,"state":[1,1,1],"y":[0,0,0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
